{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>What is this?</b> The redemption of the firstborn donkey — which is an unclean animal, so that the sanctity of the body does not apply to it — and the breaking of its neck if you do not redeem it." "<b>By strength of hand YHWH brought us out of Egypt.</b> By the strength of the Egyptians' own hand YHWH brought us out, as it says: וַתֶּחֱזַק מִצְרַיִם עַל הָעָם (Exodus 12:33) — so that we could not carry our goods on wagons after the Egyptian manner, and were forced to carry them on donkeys. And a miracle was performed for them in that they sufficed for this in but a moment, and some sanctity worthy of redemption rested upon them."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:20.375451648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}